{title: 117 - The Advent of Our God}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #117 • FESTAL SONG • 12.14}
{lyricist: Charles Coffin}
{composer: William H. Walter}
{key: A}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 117}
{meta: tune FESTAL SONG}
{meta: meter 12.14}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]The [A]advent [C#m]of [A]our [D]God [A]With [D]eager [A]prayers [E/B]we [Bm]greet,
[E]And [A]singing [E/G#]haste [D/F#]upon [Bm/D]His [E]road [C#m]His [D]coming [A/C#]reign [E]to [E7]meet.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]The everlasting Son
[E]Was born [A]to make [D]us [E/B]free;
[E]And He [D/F#]a [Bm/D]servant's [D]form [A/C#]put [E7]on
[E]To gain [A/E]our [E]liberty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[E]As Judge, [A]on clouds [D]of [E/B]light,
[E]He soon [A]will come [D]again,
[E]His scattered [Bm/D]people [D]to [A/C#]unite
[E]With them [D/F#]in [Bm/D]heaven [D]to [E]reign.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[E]Praise [A]to [C#m]the [D]incarnate [Bm]Son
[E]Who [A]comes [D]to set [A]us [Bm]free,
[E]With Father, [Bm/D]Spirit, [D]ever [E7]one,
[E]To all [A/E]eternity.
{end_of_verse}
